# What is NSG?

NSG (Network Security Group) is Azure firewall-like security layer.

NSG controls:

* Which traffic allowed
* Which traffic denied
* Which ports open
* Which source allowed
* Which destination allowed

---

# Important NSG Concepts

| Concept       | Meaning                        |
| ------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Inbound Rule  | Incoming traffic               |
| Outbound Rule | Outgoing traffic               |
| Source        | Traffic kaha se aa raha        |
| Destination   | Traffic kahan ja raha          |
| Port          | Kaunsi application/service     |
| Priority      | Kaunsa rule pehle execute hoga |
| Allow/Deny    | Traffic permit/block           |

---

# IMPORTANT RULE

```text
Lower Priority Number = Higher Preference
```

Example:

| Priority | Execution Order |
| -------- | --------------- |
| 100      | First           |
| 120      | Second          |
| 65000    | Later           |

---

# Actual NSG Rules Used

| Priority | Rule Name                     | Source            | Port | Purpose                 |
| -------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------- | ---- | ----------------------- |
| 100      | allow-ssh-admin               | 10.0.4.0/24       | 22   | SSH only from Admin VM  |
| 120      | allow-https-from-loadbalancer | AzureLoadBalancer | 443  | Health Probe            |
| 130      | allow-https-any               | Any               | 443  | Public HTTPS Traffic    |
| 65500    | DenyAllInbound                | Any               | Any  | Block remaining traffic |

