# Biggest Confusion

Question:

```text
Agar public user Load Balancer par aa raha hai,
then AzureLoadBalancer rule kyu?
Aur Any rule kyu?
```

---

# VERY IMPORTANT CONCEPT

Azure Load Balancer me 2 alag traffic types hote hain:

| Traffic Type         | Source Seen in NSG |
| -------------------- | ------------------ |
| Real User Traffic    | Internet / Any     |
| Health Probe Traffic | AzureLoadBalancer  |

---

# 1. Real User Traffic

Example:

User browser me open karta hai:

```text
https://erp.spinfra.in
```

Flow:

```text
Laptop
   ↓
Internet
   ↓
Azure Load Balancer
   ↓
Backend VM
```

NSG ko source dikhega:

```text
Internet
```

NOT:

```text
AzureLoadBalancer
```

Isliye ye rule mandatory hai:

| Source | Port |
| ------ | ---- |
| Any    | 443  |

---

# 2. Health Probe Traffic

Azure Load Balancer continuously backend VM health check karta hai.

Question:

```text
"Backend VM alive hai ya nahi?"
```

Flow:

```text
Azure LB Health Probe
   ↓
Backend VM
```

NSG source dikhega:

```text
AzureLoadBalancer
```

Isliye ye rule mandatory hai:

| Source            | Port |
| ----------------- | ---- |
| AzureLoadBalancer | 443  |

---

# IMPORTANT UNDERSTANDING

## Public Traffic Port

Controls:

```text
Internet users ka traffic
```

---

## Health Probe Port

Controls:

```text
Internal LB backend health checking
```

Both can be DIFFERENT.

---

# Why Probe Port Was 443?

Because health probe itself configured tha:

| Setting  | Value |
| -------- | ----- |
| Protocol | TCP   |
| Port     | 443   |

Azure LB internally every 5 seconds check kar raha tha:

```text
Can I connect to VM on port 443?
```

---

# VERY IMPORTANT

This does NOT mean:

```text
Public HTTPS validation
```

It only means:

```text
TCP connectivity check on 443
```

---

# Could Probe Use Port 80?

YES absolutely.

Example:

| Component           | Port |
| ------------------- | ---- |
| Public User Traffic | 443  |
| Health Probe        | 80   |

This is common enterprise setup.

---

# Example Enterprise Design

```text
Internet User
   ↓
HTTPS 443
   ↓
Load Balancer
   ↓
Backend App
```

Health Probe:

```text
HTTP GET /health on port 80
```

---

# Probe Types Explained

| Probe Type  | What It Checks        |
| ----------- | --------------------- |
| TCP Probe   | Only port open?       |
| HTTP Probe  | Valid HTTP response?  |
| HTTPS Probe | Valid HTTPS response? |

---

# Your Current Probe

| Setting  | Value |
| -------- | ----- |
| Protocol | TCP   |
| Port     | 443   |

Meaning:

```text
Only TCP connectivity check
```

NOT SSL validation.

---

# Why Only AzureLoadBalancer Rule Was NOT Enough

Initially:

| Rule                    | Status  |
| ----------------------- | ------- |
| AzureLoadBalancer → 443 | Allowed |
| Internet → 443          | Missing |

Result:

```text
Health probe successful
Backend healthy
```

BUT:

```text
Real users blocked
```

Browser error:

```text
ERR_CONNECTION_TIMED_OUT
```

---

# Why Internet Rule Was Required

Real users appear in NSG as:

```text
Internet
```

NOT:

```text
AzureLoadBalancer
```

Therefore this rule mandatory tha:

| Source | Port |
| ------ | ---- |
| Any    | 443  |

---

# Important Azure Standard Load Balancer Behavior

Standard SKU Load Balancer is:

```text
Secure by Default
```

Meaning:

Even if:

* Public IP exists
* LB exists
* Backend healthy exists

Traffic still blocked rahega unless NSG explicitly allow kare.

---

# Default NSG Rules

Azure automatically kuch default rules create karta hai.

Example:

| Rule                          | Purpose               |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------- |
| AllowVnetInBound              | VNet internal traffic |
| AllowAzureLoadBalancerInBound | Azure LB traffic      |
| DenyAllInbound                | Block everything else |

---

# Why Custom Rules Better?

Default AzureLoadBalancer rule allows:

```text
ALL ports
ALL protocols
```

Better approach:

```text
Only required ports allow karo
```

Example:

| Source            | Port     |
| ----------------- | -------- |
| AzureLoadBalancer | 443 only |

More secure.

---

# Final Production-Grade Architecture

| Rule                    | Purpose               |
| ----------------------- | --------------------- |
| SSH only from Jump VM   | Secure administration |
| AzureLoadBalancer → 443 | Health Probe          |
| Any → 443               | Public HTTPS          |
| Deny SSH from Internet  | Security              |

